 "note": "THE POOL, FOUR WAYS (only with &seq=pool&opt=A, B, C or D). The swipe on from 'from' is the visitor's last act; the steps then play by themselves and control comes back after the last. Per step: 'in' = how the picture arrives: 'cut' (simply there), 'dissolve' (over 'ms'), or 'black' (the screen goes black for 'ms', then the picture comes up over 'up' ms); the first step's 'in' is the swipe itself. 'hold' = ms it stays. 'depth' = how much the picture answers the hand (1 = as normal, 0 = frozen flat); 'ease' = ms to get there (otherwise at once). 'soft' = the background falls out of focus, the near stays sharp. 'shade' = how dark (0 to 1). 'breath' = the one movement: after 'still' ms, the depth slowly returns and the view drifts once and rests ('breath' below: how far). 'restoreMs' = how long the hand's control takes to come fully back at the end. 'push' = [from, to]: how far the view is carried forward through the depth across the picture's hold, accelerating (near things grow, far ones barely). 'land' = ms for the push to run out and come to rest, slowly and heavily. 'drift' (per option) = the viewpoint moving on its own along one unbroken path through every picture, so the depth maps carry the motion: 'from' and 'to' = where it starts and ends [x, y] (-1 to 1, as far as the depth goes), 'sway' = how far it bows on the way, 'settle' = ms it takes to come to rest at 016, 'handBack' = ms for the visitor's hand to take over again. 'zoom' = [from, to] how many times closer the view is (1 = the whole picture), 'zoomAt' = the point it closes in on [x, y] (0 to 1 across the picture), 'zoomMs' = how long (otherwise the hold); with 'land' it opens out, slowing to rest. Per option: 'look' = the aged-print amounts for the whole passage (as the sliders: tone, fade, grain, specks, scratches, dust, foxing), 'lookIn' / 'lookOut' = ms to go in and to come back to the sliders; 'noLunge' = no zoom on the swipe out of 013. F/G/H: restrained studies without aged-print overlays or pushes. All rooms preload at 013. F removes an interval; G uses a small continuous lateral drift; H holds the central moment while surrounding events rush past. G-original preserves One photo set. depthMove: signed, gentle camera travel through the actual depth maps, in dolly units over the hold; reset on each restrained cut. Suppressed for reduced motion.",
